      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Directional coronary atherectomy is emerging as the treatment of choice for many patients with significant lesions involving left anterior descending coronary artery origin or vessel bifurcations. It offers the potential advantages of safe, reliable, and predictable treatment of these selected complex lesions. Future modifications and improvements in the design of the atherectomy device (AtheroCath; Devices for Vascular Intervention, Redwood City, CA) may further expand its application to smaller and calcified vessels."},
